            <ArticleTitle>Gastric duplication cyst: a rare entity.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1093/jscr/rjw073</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">rjw073</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Gastric duplication cysts are an uncommon finding, especially in the adult population. Presenting symptoms can be non-specific, but can include abdominal pain, nausea and emesis. In this report, we present a 28-year-old female diagnosed with a communicating gastric cyst with both gastric and duodenal mucosa, along with pancreatic tissue and no evidence of dysplasia or malignancy. The clinical picture, diagnosis and treatment are described and compared to findings in the literature.</AbstractText>
